  "reference_note": "Access documents country/region-dependent DBCS spaces; the Microsoft CP932 mapping assigns byte pair 0x8140 to U+3000. This motivates the explicit Japanese rule without claiming native runtime comparison evidence.",
  "contracts": [
    "Only explicit Japanese casing language adds ideographic space to the existing ASCII separators. Exact LCID 1041 and host-selected Japanese use the same service; explicit English overrides remain authoritative.",
    "Separators, empty segments and unrelated characters are preserved. No general Unicode whitespace splitting, normalization, locale discovery or additional numeric LCID aliases.",
    "Locale checks, raw-range publication, parameterized plan reuse and encoding/width composition keep their existing boundaries.",
    "A seven-byte source expands to eight bytes before later narrowing to six; its seven-byte intermediate cap still fails. Sink errors and every observed kernel/evaluator cancellation checkpoint propagate.",
    "No dependency, runtime, stored type, default allowance or write qualification changes. Broader DBCS cultures and native word-start/NLS behavior remain open.",
    "Reference models now select the Japanese delimiter explicitly; original default ASCII callers keep their prior model. The next combined replay includes new Japanese word cases and composed native fields."
  ],
